<article class="env-remark" id="05TZ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TZ">Remark <span data-tag="05TZ">7.7.2.21</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a simplicial set, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which admits pullbacks and $K$-indexed colimits, and let $F: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a diagram. Stated more informally, Remark <a data-tag="05TY" href="/tag/05TY">7.7.2.20</a> asserts that the colimit of $F$ is strongly universal if and only if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(a')$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every morphism $C' \rightarrow C = \varinjlim (F)$ in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the comparison map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \varinjlim _{x \in K}( C' \times _{C} F(x) ) \rightarrow C' \times _{C} \varinjlim _{x \in K}( F(x) ) \simeq C' \]
</div>
<p>
 is an isomorphism. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(b')$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every cartesian natural transformation $\gamma : F' \rightarrow F$, the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ F'(x) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \varinjlim (F) \ar [d] \\ F(x) \ar [r] &amp;  \varinjlim (F) } \]
</div>
<p>
 is a pullback square for each vertex $x \in K$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article>
